      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay that makes more sense, thanks. so if the frequency goes up, the reactance goes down and more current flows through, right? i think i get the math now. could you just give me one more quick example of how this would look in a real-world circuit? like, if i'm looking at a filter or something?",
